# Upload filter for `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# gcloud does NOT read .dockerignore — without this file it would upload the
# whole tree, including ui/node_modules (~3 GB) and venv (~1 GB).
#
# IMPORTANT: this uses .gitignore syntax, where a bare name like `run` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth. That silently dropped
# ui/src/app/workflow/[workflowId]/run and pipecat/src/pipecat/evals from an
# earlier upload and broke the build with a confusing "Module not found".
# Every repo-root-only entry below is therefore anchored with a leading slash.

.git
.github
.gcloudignore

# Local environments (anchored — do not match nested dirs)
/venv
/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
/.mypy_cache
/.pytest_cache
/.ruff_cache

# Local runtime state (anchored: `run`, `logs` and `certs` all exist as
# legitimate source directories deeper in the tree)
/logs
/run
/certs
/dograh_pcm_cache
/failte_voice_previews

# Not needed by any image (anchored: pipecat/src/pipecat/evals IS needed)
/evals
/sdk
/app-doc

# Never upload secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
/deploy/gcp/secrets
